WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:00.900
Maggie Haberman,

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:03.203
you're you're reporting on on all of this

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:04.471
leading up to the bombshell

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:05.972
reporting that we just got

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:06.840
from Paula

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.608
in terms of how the president's team

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:12.312
may defend this

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:14.314
I don't think they quite know

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:15.949
how to defend

00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:18.018
this, Poppy, from what we have heard.

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:18.318
You know,

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:18.852
they were,

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:20.220
as Kaitlan said,

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.054
very startled

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:22.422
by the existence of this tape.

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:23.456
This tape

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.026
was something that they learned existed

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:28.128
when this aide to Trump testified

00:00:28.361 --> 00:00:28.962
the prosecutors

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:30.897
were already in possession of this tape.

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:31.231
They didn't

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:32.565
get it from the aide,

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:34.234
although it appears the aide had a copy

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:35.835
when it was subpoenaed later.

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:37.670
But this is and has been described

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:38.038
to us

00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:39.339
this way by multiple sources

00:00:39.339 --> 00:00:40.974
since you guys broke this incredible

00:00:40.974 --> 00:00:43.009
piece of reporting many days ago

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:46.780
as a really problematic piece of evidence

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:47.747
for Trump.

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:48.748
Now, I think they're going to

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:49.883
stick to their line of,

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:50.216
you know,

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:51.184
he says things

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:53.453
he didn't mean it a certain way.

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:53.787
You know, I'm

00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:54.821
sure that they can come up

00:00:54.821 --> 00:00:56.322
with all kinds of explanations

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:58.191
for why he used the language he used.

00:00:58.191 --> 00:00:59.659
But it's on tape.

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:00.326
And one of the things

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:01.394
that's really striking Poppy,

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:02.429
about this to me again, is

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:03.863
this is someone Donald Trump,

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:05.498
who is incredibly paranoid over

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:07.600
many decades about people taking notes

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:08.902
of what he says

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:09.936
and people taking notes

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:11.037
of what he's doing

00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:12.405
And here he is

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:13.206
with people

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:14.474
because he also has a habit

00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:15.542
of showing off

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:17.210
when he's in certain meetings

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:18.745
and trying to, you know,

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:19.946
sort of puff himself up.

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:20.880
And that

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.282
is what many people close to him

00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:22.649
said to me

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:24.384
they thought he was doing in this tape.

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:26.386
And it's not as if he didn't know,

00:01:26.386 --> 00:01:28.221
you know, tapes or audio

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:29.756
recordings were rolling.

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:31.391
He knew what he was doing

00:01:31.391 --> 00:01:33.393
and he went ahead and just said this.

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:34.027
So, look,

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:35.095
we don't know whether this will be

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:36.062
part of a criminal complaint,

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:37.831
but there's every reason to assume

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:38.364
this would be

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:39.432
because it's been said to me

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:40.200
by several people

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.302
this is the most significant

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:43.770
piece of evidence that they know of that

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:44.671
the government has,

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:44.871
you know,

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:46.473
even the idea of the evidence

00:01:46.473 --> 00:01:48.675
or the various pieces of evidence

00:01:48.675 --> 00:01:50.310
that could end up in this indictment.

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:51.044
We haven't heard

00:01:51.044 --> 00:01:52.112
from the Justice Department.

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:53.246
The prison former president

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:54.614
announced the indictment.

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:55.381
His legal team doesn't

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:56.282
have the indictment.

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:57.951
As far as we know. We don't either.

00:01:58.952 --> 00:01:59.352
But get

00:01:59.352 --> 00:01:59.619
it that

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:00.186
point the

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:02.555
idea of there seems to be between

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:03.823
tapes, between phones,

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:06.926
between obviously the the witnesses.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:08.628
There's a lot to work with

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:10.930
for what they're putting together.

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:12.165
Yes, there is

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:13.733
there is a lot to work with.

00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:14.868
And one of the things I think

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:16.703
we're looking for this morning,

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:19.205
if the Justice Department goes to a judge

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:21.441
and gets to release this

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:23.209
this indictment, the criminal complaint

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:25.145
against the former president.

00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:27.480
What we're expecting to see

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.549
is what they call

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:30.416
a speaking indictment,

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:31.351
an indictment

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:34.721
that tells a narrative that really gives

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:36.489
a lot of the information

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:38.791
that they believe proves

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:40.360
why the former president,

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:41.161
the former president

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:42.362
should be

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:43.163
found guilty

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:44.898
of violating multiple,

00:02:44.898 --> 00:02:46.533
multiple criminal laws.

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:48.568
And if they don't do that,

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:50.336
if this criminal

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.505
indictment, if this criminal information

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:54.140
that they put out

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:56.509
doesn't have those details at the start,

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:57.911
I think what it does

00:02:57.911 --> 00:03:00.280
is it helps give the former president

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:03.349
certainly continue to have the field

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:04.551
to be able to mold

00:03:04.551 --> 00:03:05.685
and drive

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:06.886
the narrative about what

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:07.754
this case is about.

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:09.255
He's already doing that.

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:11.157
He's already doing that. And the

00:03:12.192 --> 00:03:13.259
fact is that the Justice

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:14.594
Department probably,

00:03:14.594 --> 00:03:15.028
you know,

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:16.829
if they had done this the right way,

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:18.531
they would have they should have

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:19.832
had a judge already

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:22.068
sign off on releasing this last night

00:03:22.302 --> 00:03:24.904
so that the public can see what it is

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:27.273
behind these charges now.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.375
Here's the deal about this.

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:29.909
This tape,

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:30.877
it is possible

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:32.145
that they might not mention it

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:34.414
in the criminal complaint,

00:03:34.414 --> 00:03:36.182
but but I would bet

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:37.617
that they at some point

00:03:37.617 --> 00:03:39.085
when this goes to trial,

00:03:39.085 --> 00:03:40.453
that they will present this

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:41.888
because it will be proof

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:43.156
even is that the fact that,

00:03:43.156 --> 00:03:43.389
you know,

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:43.656
the former

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:45.291
president didn't do classified things.

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:45.892
Right.

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:47.327
What they want to prove

00:03:47.327 --> 00:03:49.929
is that the former president knew

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:51.931
these things were national

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:52.865
defense information.

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:54.767
And one way you prove it is by saying

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:56.603
these things are classified.

00:03:56.603 --> 00:03:57.337
And the president

00:03:57.337 --> 00:03:58.805
the former president knew that.

00:03:58.805 --> 00:03:59.839
And so you can bet

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:01.274
that this is going to be part

00:04:01.274 --> 00:04:02.809
of the criminal case.

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:06.179
Paula, your lawyer, it's most apparent,

00:04:06.179 --> 00:04:07.146
I think, to everyone

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:08.581
this could tie in to

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:09.816
the first charge

00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:10.917
were willful retention

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:12.452
of defense information.

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:13.353
What I'm interested in

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:14.387
is your perspective on

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:15.421
if you could think this could

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:16.923
play into the latter

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:18.224
charges, especially obstruction

00:04:18.224 --> 00:04:19.225
and false statements

00:04:19.225 --> 00:04:20.393
and the timeline

00:04:20.393 --> 00:04:22.328
because this is a recording from 20, 21.

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:24.030
So he's already out of office.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:26.799
So what should we consider

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:27.967
around that until at least

00:04:27.967 --> 00:04:30.136
we see the unsealed indictment?

00:04:30.136 --> 00:04:31.504
It's a great question, Poppy.

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:33.273
Look, when when we broke this story

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:34.707
last week, it really change.

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:34.874
I know

00:04:34.874 --> 00:04:36.242
my personal understanding

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:38.544
of this investigation, Katelyn, Caitlin,

00:04:38.544 --> 00:04:40.213
Evan, our competition, Maggie

00:04:40.213 --> 00:04:41.381
and I, we've all been reporting on this

00:04:41.381 --> 00:04:42.582
for a really long time.

00:04:42.582 --> 00:04:43.549
And it wasn't clear to me

00:04:43.549 --> 00:04:44.350
that the former president

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:45.852
was absolutely going to be charged.

00:04:45.852 --> 00:04:47.120
And if he was charged,

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:48.421
what they could possibly charge him

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:50.123
with beyond obstruction.

00:04:50.123 --> 00:04:52.325
But once we got this recording,

00:04:52.325 --> 00:04:53.092
it was so clear

00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:54.627
that this was going to be a key

00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:55.261
piece of evidence.

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:56.129
I didn't use a legal team

00:04:56.129 --> 00:04:56.729
to tell me that.

00:04:56.729 --> 00:04:58.364
It was pretty obvious because in here

00:04:58.364 --> 00:05:00.333
he is admitting in his own words

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:01.167
this is a recording.

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:02.201
This is the one of the most

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:03.269
damning kinds of evidence

00:05:03.269 --> 00:05:04.037
that a prosecutor

00:05:04.037 --> 00:05:06.039
can have against someone.

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:07.173
He is admitting that

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:08.308
he willingly,

00:05:08.308 --> 00:05:11.544
knowingly retained secret information.

00:05:11.577 --> 00:05:12.545
He seems a little confused

00:05:12.545 --> 00:05:14.180
about the classification level

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:15.615
of this alleged document.

00:05:15.615 --> 00:05:17.917
But that is incredibly damning.

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:19.118
We also don't know where

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:20.119
this document is,

00:05:20.119 --> 00:05:21.888
so I am sure that prosecutors

00:05:21.888 --> 00:05:23.890
are working on that. Why?

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:25.258
If they have if they don't have it back,

00:05:25.258 --> 00:05:26.793
why they don't have it back.

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:28.061
But then also the fact

00:05:28.061 --> 00:05:30.163
that he's undercutting his own claim

00:05:30.163 --> 00:05:30.763
of his power

00:05:30.763 --> 00:05:31.831
to declassify stuff

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:33.833
at any point in this investigation.

00:05:33.833 --> 00:05:35.001
They've argued that, again,

00:05:35.001 --> 00:05:36.035
to prosecutors

00:05:36.035 --> 00:05:37.737
that they didn't have to return something

00:05:37.737 --> 00:05:39.138
because he had declassified it.

00:05:39.138 --> 00:05:39.272
Well,

00:05:39.272 --> 00:05:40.640
this completely undercuts

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:42.542
that and could potentially go

00:05:42.542 --> 00:05:43.543
to obstruction.

00:05:43.543 --> 00:05:44.644
But it will be interesting to see

00:05:44.644 --> 00:05:46.179
we don't know at this point

00:05:46.179 --> 00:05:47.180
how this recording

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:48.348
will factor into the indictment,

00:05:48.348 --> 00:05:48.981
but it's clear it's

00:05:48.981 --> 00:05:50.049
one of the most valuable

00:05:50.049 --> 00:05:51.417
pieces of evidence.

00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:52.418
And as we've reported

00:05:52.418 --> 00:05:53.820
before, this really changed

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:54.854
our entire understanding

00:05:54.854 --> 00:05:56.189
of this investigation.

00:05:56.189 --> 00:05:57.390
The time. Right.

00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:58.191
The place

00:05:58.191 --> 00:05:59.559
and the kind of evidence

00:05:59.559 --> 00:06:00.827
I mean, the time this goes all the way

00:06:00.827 --> 00:06:03.062
back to the summer of 20, 21,

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:03.730
almost a year

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:05.398
before the search of Mar a Lago.

00:06:05.398 --> 00:06:06.432
This is the kind of evidence

00:06:06.432 --> 00:06:07.233
that they have.

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:08.701
Remember, he's at Bedminster.

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:09.736
Up until now,

00:06:09.736 --> 00:06:10.136
we didn't

00:06:10.136 --> 00:06:10.403
believe that

00:06:10.403 --> 00:06:11.938
there were any classified documents

00:06:11.938 --> 00:06:13.973
that had been found at Bedminster.

00:06:13.973 --> 00:06:15.408
So this takes this into yet

00:06:15.408 --> 00:06:16.876
another theater.

00:06:16.876 --> 00:06:18.144
And then lastly,

00:06:18.144 --> 00:06:19.712
I alluded to this,

00:06:19.712 --> 00:06:20.446
the former president,

00:06:20.446 --> 00:06:21.681
as someone who's very careful

00:06:21.681 --> 00:06:22.982
not to email, not a text

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:24.450
that has really been an obstacle

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:25.952
in previous investigations.

00:06:25.952 --> 00:06:27.420
They didn't have the kind of evidence

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:28.354
that they needed

00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:30.490
to tie him to any alleged crimes.

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:31.991
And here really arguably

00:06:31.991 --> 00:06:33.593
for probably one of the first times

00:06:33.593 --> 00:06:34.761
they have this recording

00:06:34.761 --> 00:06:36.562
and it is so incredibly damning.

00:06:36.562 --> 00:06:37.697
So we're waiting to see if

00:06:37.697 --> 00:06:38.765
and when the Justice Department

00:06:38.765 --> 00:06:40.466
unsealed this indictment,

00:06:40.466 --> 00:06:41.501
how this factors in.

00:06:41.501 --> 00:06:42.769
But it will likely be a key

00:06:42.769 --> 00:06:43.503
piece of evidence.

00:06:43.503 --> 00:06:44.404
It's the strongest thing

00:06:44.404 --> 00:06:45.705
we know from our reporting

00:06:45.705 --> 00:06:46.706
that they have so far.

00:06:46.706 --> 00:06:47.907
Thanks to your reporting.

00:06:47.907 --> 00:06:49.142
Now, the American public,

00:06:49.142 --> 00:06:51.644
everyone knows the president's own words

00:06:51.811 --> 00:06:53.079
from allies to current

00:06:53.079 --> 00:06:53.913
political opponents,

00:06:53.913 --> 00:06:55.415
Republicans are largely coming

00:06:55.415 --> 00:06:57.216
to Donald Trump's defense this morning.

00:06:57.216 --> 00:06:58.317
House Speaker Kevin McCarthy,

00:06:58.317 --> 00:07:00.319
for one, calling it a dark day

00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:02.321
for the United States, saying on Twitter,

00:07:02.321 --> 00:07:03.556
releasing a statement saying that

00:07:03.556 --> 00:07:05.091
he stands with Donald Trump

00:07:05.091 --> 00:07:05.658
against what

00:07:05.658 --> 00:07:08.094
McCarthy calls a grave injustice

00:07:08.428 --> 00:07:09.695
and also promising,

00:07:09.695 --> 00:07:10.563
quote, House

00:07:10.563 --> 00:07:11.197
Republicans

00:07:11.197 --> 00:07:12.365
will hold this brazen

00:07:12.365 --> 00:07:14.667
weaponization of power accountable

00:07:15.001 --> 00:07:16.235
Now, campaign rival

00:07:16.235 --> 00:07:17.036
Ron DeSantis,

00:07:17.036 --> 00:07:18.438
he said something very similar,

00:07:18.438 --> 00:07:19.872
tweeting this The weaponization

00:07:19.872 --> 00:07:21.507
of federal law enforcement represents

00:07:21.507 --> 00:07:23.810
a mortal threat to a free society.

